  "answer": "For a new HTTP status code, first check whether the project’s status-code registry already includes it. If it does not, add the numeric code and its canonical name and useful aliases in `requests/status_codes.py` (the file is not among the excerpts). Add or update tests to check that `requests.codes` resolves the name and aliases to the number, then run the test suite and submit a pull request with a concise explanation and a link to the relevant HTTP specification or authoritative source. The shown `adapters.py` code already copies the server’s status into `Response.status_code`; you generally do not need to change it. Change `sessions.py` only if the new code should affect redirect behavior—the listed redirect codes are handled specially at lines 224–227. The digest-auth range check in `auth.py` covers all 4xx responses, so a new 4xx code generally needs no change there.",
